# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  phonassoc.la — ⊕ IS ASSOCIATIVE IN THE PHONETIC REGISTER, and the
#  algebra says it must not be. This module WITNESSES that bound.
#
#  ── THE COLLAPSE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  CONP renders ⊕ as `A ++ 960 zeros ++ B`. Concatenation with a fixed
#  separator is associative, so
#      ⊕(⊕(A,B),C)  and  ⊕(A,⊕(B,C))
#  both render `A ++ Z ++ B ++ Z ++ C`. Not similar — THE SAME SEQUENCE.
#  It is a structural identity, not a detection difficulty: there is one
#  object, so no detector could ever separate them.
#
#  ── WHY THAT IS A BOUND AND NOT A CURIOSITY ────────────────────────
#  The paper: "G IS the free magma on nine generators … NON-ASSOCIATIVE
#  because grouping IS etymology", and "(a⊗b)⊗c and a⊗(b⊗c) record
#  different derivations and therefore are different concepts. An
#  associative algebra would erase the etymology the seal exists to
#  carry." A free magma is non-associative in ALL its operations. So the
#  phonetic register identifies two terms the algebra declares distinct.
#
#  ── ★ WHAT KIND OF BOUND THIS IS, stated precisely ─────────────────
#  NOT the same kind as ⊕/VOID. There, ⊕'s inserted /ʔ/ closure and
#  VOID's breath silence are the SAME ACOUSTIC EVENT — nothing exists to
#  separate, and no rendering could. Here a bracketing marker IS
#  constructible: a depth cue in the closure would separate them.
#  ⇒ This is a bound BY RULING (Erik, 2026-09-05), not by acoustics: the
#  cue was declined because it changes the phonology and the gated WAV
#  outputs. Recording it as acoustically irreducible would be a stronger
#  claim than the evidence supports, so it is recorded as what it is.
#
#  ── SCOPE ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Affects every ⊕ compound of depth ≥ 2. Bounds the PHONETIC register
#  ONLY — κ still inverts and the glyphic round trip is untouched.
#
#  ★ IF THIS GATE GOES RED, THE BOUND MOVED. A red here means the two
#  bracketings stopped rendering identically — i.e. someone added the
#  bracketing marker. That is the bound being LIFTED, and it should be
#  celebrated and re-witnessed, not silenced by editing the expectation.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

import("phonym.la")

glyph TRUE = la t. la f. t
glyph FALSE= la t. la f. f
glyph IF   = la c. la t. la f. c(t)(f)("!")
glyph NOT  = la b. b(FALSE)(TRUE)
glyph Z    = la f. (la x. f(la v. x(x)(v)))(la x. f(la v. x(x)(v)))

glyph A = PRIM("BEING")
glyph B = PRIM("VOID")
glyph C = PRIM("FORM")

# first index at which two signals differ, or -1 if identical throughout
glyph FIRSTDIFF = Z(la self. la p. la q. la i.
    IF(NOT(lt(i)(FST(p))))(la _. sub(0)(1))(la _.
    IF(int_eq(SND(p)(i))(SND(q)(i)))(la _. self(p)(q)(add(i)(1)))(la _. i)))

glyph CMP = la p. la q.
    IF(int_eq(FST(p))(FST(q)))(la _. int_to_str(FIRSTDIFF(p)(q)(0)))
                              (la _. "len-differs")

# THE BOUND: the two bracketings of ⊕
glyph LB = PHONYM(CON(CON(A)(B))(C))
glyph RB = PHONYM(CON(A)(CON(B)(C)))

# ★ THE CONTROL, and it is what makes the line above mean anything. A
#   FIRSTDIFF stuck at -1 would report every pair identical and look
#   exactly like a bound. ⊕(A,B) and ⊕(B,A) have the SAME LENGTH and
#   MUST differ — ⊕ is not commutative — so the comparator is required
#   to produce a non-negative index here.
glyph SW1 = PHONYM(CON(A)(B))
glyph SW2 = PHONYM(CON(B)(A))

glyph SEQ2 = la a. la b. b
glyph MAIN =
  SEQ2(print(concat("assoc  lenL=")(concat(int_to_str(FST(LB)))(
       concat(" lenR=")(concat(int_to_str(FST(RB)))(
       concat(" firstdiff=")(CMP(LB)(RB))))))))(
       print(concat("control(swap) lenX=")(concat(int_to_str(FST(SW1)))(
       concat(" lenY=")(concat(int_to_str(FST(SW2)))(
       concat(" firstdiff=")(CMP(SW1)(SW2))))))))
